bibliograph-happyview (2.17.4-5) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Packaging revision 5: the deploy oneshot bounds the runtime role's
    connections and drops an index that only cost inserts. The HappyView
    binary is unchanged at 2.17.4.

    - `sql/role-limits.sql` is applied by `hv-deploy` on every run, including
      with `--no-indexes`: `ALTER ROLE happyview_app CONNECTION LIMIT 40` and
      `idle_session_timeout = 120s`, after a network backfill was measured
      holding 71 idle backends on a cluster whose `max_connections` is 100.
      Both need a superuser; when `hv-deploy` connects as `bibliograph` the
      file raises a notice and the postgres role applies them from Ansible.
    - `sql/indexes.sql` drops `happyview_record_review_identifiers_idx`: a GIN
      index over an expression on a `text` column, 0 scans on a 371k-row table
      while `INSERT INTO happyview_records` spent ~2.9s mean.
    - `build-deb.sh` installs `happyview/sql/*.sql` by glob instead of naming
      three files, so a new file cannot ship missing and crash `hv-deploy`
      after it has uploaded the lexicons.

 -- Bibliograph Maintainers <maintainers@olamaelcu.net>  Wed, 18 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000

bibliograph-happyview (2.17.4-4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Packaging revision 4: the network backfill a first registration could
    start is opt-in. The HappyView binary is unchanged at 2.17.4.

    - Revision 3 registered Popfeed's two record collections with
      `backfill: true`, so the first upload asked HappyView to crawl every repo
      writing them — thousands on the production network. On a live host that
      crawl held 89 of 100 Postgres slots with load past 50, and the deploy's
      own catalog pass died of a lock timeout behind it.
    - `hv-deploy` now requests the backfill only when `HV_BACKFILL_LEXICONS` is
      set (`1`/`true`/`yes`). Registering the collections still happens on
      every run; only the crawl is opt-in, and HappyView starts one on the
      first upload alone, so a re-deploy requests nothing either way.

 -- Bibliograph Maintainers <maintainers@olamaelcu.net>  Tue, 17 Nov 2026 22:53:25 +0000

bibliograph-happyview (2.17.4-3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Packaging revision 3: carry Popfeed's book lexicons and register their
    collections. The HappyView binary is unchanged at 2.17.4.

    - `happyview/lexicons/social/popfeed/` adds `feed.review`, `feed.listItem`
      and `richtext.facet`, the document `feed.review.facets` refs. Three
      fields are loosened from Popfeed's published schemas because live
      records violate them: `mainCreditRole` becomes `knownValues` ("Written
      by"), and `genres.items.maxLength` and `releaseDate.format` are dropped.
      Nothing is published under our DID: the namespace is Popfeed's, so
      `publish-lexicons.mjs` skips it.
    - The deploy oneshot registers both record collections and the `defs`
      document, and asks HappyView for a network backfill on the first upload:
      the records predate the upload, and Jetstream only carries new activity.

 -- Bibliograph Maintainers <maintainers@olamaelcu.net>  Tue, 17 Nov 2026 22:28:46 +0000

